{
  "program": "CBSTM03B",
  "caseId": "case19",
  "description": "WHEN OTHER GO TO 9999-GOBACK - app/cbl/CBSTM03B.CBL:127-131, gate G48. The GO TO jumps past every nnn900-EXIT, so no MOVE <dd>FILE-STATUS TO LK-M03B-RC runs at all and LK-M03B-RC and LK-M03B-FLDT still hold exactly what the caller left there. Asserting that requires a stale value worth recognising, so the run first browses XREFFILE to end of file, leaving '10' in the caller's own LK-M03B-RC and the last record in the area, and then calls with an unrecognised DD name WITHOUT re-issuing MOVE ZERO TO WS-M03B-RC. The answer is '10' and that same record - the STALE prior value, not a '00' and not an invented error status. The final call repeats the point with an 'O' operation to show the arm is chosen by the DD name alone: a perfectly valid operation against an unknown DD is still nothing at all.",
